/T (The King's answer is separation. The gates of the castle are closed, the staff sent away, and Elsa is taken from her sister and taught to hide what she is: conceal it, don't feel it, don't let it show. Anna, remembering nothing, spends her childhood knocking at a door that never opens, growing up in an empty castle beside a sister who will not look at her.)
